[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"People who lose a loved one to suicide, accident, or homicide should seek professional help rather than trying to cope alone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"In the first six months after losing a spouse, assign one trusted person to oversee meals, sleep, medication for chronic conditions, and follow‑up appointments"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"For those without family or friends, replace “the person watching over you” with three simple things: a neighbor who can enter your home, a spot on the community outreach list, and emergency contacts saved on your phone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After a parent dies, tell the child the truth, let him attend the funeral, and don’t send him to another environment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Still stuck in grief after half a year, unable to move on — when to see a psychiatrist or clinical psychologist"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Don’t spend money on grief counseling right away — first check whether your grief is truly stuck (see the symptoms listed in item 8)"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Don’t drop yibao or turn to alcohol after separating or divorcing"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/29-11","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Call 12356 for general support, 12355 for minors and teens; for medical care, book a psychology clinic appointment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"In the first three months after a tragedy, postpone any irreversible major decisions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Don’t treat death as a way to settle debts: life insurance won’t pay out for suicides within two years, workplace injuries won’t be recognized, and debts are still deducted from your estate first"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/29"},"children":["Chapter 29"," ·"," ","After experiencing a major setback"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"29-11"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["11"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-b"},"children":["Evidence"," ","B"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Call 12356 for general support, 12355 for minors and teens; for medical care, book a psychology clinic appointment"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["If you need someone to talk to, dial 12356 — this is the national mental health helpline, and it’s completely free. Minors and teenagers can call 12355, the dedicated youth support service. If you need professional medical care, you can book an appointment at a psychiatry, psychology, or clinical psychology clinic. Community grid workers and social workers are also expected to proactively identify people facing family issues, job loss, or school dropout."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag